NOTE ON AUTOMATED LICENSE DETECTION
GitHub identifies a licence by matching this file against a fixed corpus of
standard open-source licences (MIT, Apache-2.0, GPL, ...). This is a custom
proprietary licence, so no match is possible and GitHub will show a plain
"View license" link rather than a named licence badge. That is expected, not a
misconfiguration: making the badge appear would require replacing the text
below with a standard open-source licence, which would grant the public rights
this licence deliberately withholds. The SPDX line above is the machine-readable
marker for a non-standard licence (LicenseRef-*).

